  "about": "Our own tiledata and animdata records (cc-P26, F-8), and our worn-item animations (cc-P62, F-35), and our creature bodies (cc-P139, F-46: bodyAnims, a .vd each, into anim7 beside the worn items), and the winter decor records (cc-P34, F-22: OSI's statue 0x1224, animated fire pit 0x29FD, animated oven 0x462, tree 0xCCA and fireplace 0x45D give the flags; the statue adds Impassable; frame interval 2 as OSI's fire 0x19AB and campfire 0xDE3). Nothing here is copied from EA's files: every value is ours, and the tiledata values follow OSI's animated runestone 0xADBA 'Runestone01 Glow01' and OSI's earrings 0x1087 (flags, weight, layer and height read from the client's tiledata.mul; see SOURCE.txt). app\\Play.ps1 writes the tiledata and animdata records into copies of the player's own tiledata.mul and animdata.mul, and gives each equipAnims body a Bodyconv.def line, in a copy of the player's own Bodyconv.def, that sends it to slot 'slot' of app\\sl-anim7.bin (scripts\\build-equip-anims.py). Change only together with registry.csv. cc-P50 (F-32), the chest mimic: flags and height follow OSI's wooden chest 0xE43 (Impassable | ArticleA, without Container, since the mimic is not a container); its idle loop adds Animation, interval 4; the two dead tiles are ArticleA only.",
